In repos/activity-api/src/routes/activities.ts, add a read-only conservation-residual-trend route that reports whether each conservation residual is converging, diverging, or flat, so the substrate can observe the effect of its own repairs instead of only their current level.

Every existing self-measurement here reports a LEVEL from a snapshot: how many violations exist right now. Nothing reports MOTION: whether a residual is shrinking because a repair worked, or growing because the world is outrunning the repair. That distinction is what separates a defect worth patching from a horizon worth crossing, and it is the missing half of grading a fix on its effect rather than on whether it landed. The data already exists: each conservation auditor execution records its violation count in metadata as findings_count, giving a per-invariant time series with hundreds of samples for the busiest invariant.

