ROOT CAUSE. The observer fetches /concepts/search with NO query, which takes concept-db's relevance DESC ordering branch, and relevance is (times_succeeded + 1) / (times_loaded + 2). Ordering by relevance therefore returns precisely the concepts that HAVE successes, so a page that fills to its limit is success-biased by construction. Measured 2026-09-10: it reported total 5000, loaded 5000, loaded_with_success 5000, ratio 1.0, diagnosis "healthy", while the store held 69,142 concepts at a true ratio of 0.456 and the compose_lesson subgroup was 17 loaded / 0 ever credited. A previous attempt that only made it abstain was correctly refused as treating the symptom.

THE FIX. GET /concepts/search accepts a source_type filter (it parses query, shape, source_type, min_relevance, limit and offset). A source_type-filtered request returns a WHOLE SUBGROUP rather than the head of a global ordering, so a subgroup ratio computed that way is exact rather than sampled. compose_lesson is roughly 36 concepts, well under any page limit.

